# Applies only to builds that use the repository root as their context, which
# today is web-ui alone: every other service builds from its own directory.
#
# Without this the daemon uploads 1.1 GB for an image whose inputs are about
# 4 MB. This Docker install has no buildx, so a per-Dockerfile ignore file is
# not honoured and the exclusions have to live here.

.git
.github

# Build inputs are the lockfiles and src; installed trees and build output are
# produced inside the image and must never be copied in from the host, where
# they may carry the wrong architecture's binaries.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results

# Go and Python build artefacts.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv

# Secrets. .env is gitignored; it must not reach a build layer either.
.env
.env.*
!apps/web-ui/.env.development
!apps/web-ui/.env.live
!apps/web-ui/.env.production

# Nothing outside apps/ and packages/ is an input to the frontend build.
infra
mocks
scripts
services
tools
db
docs

*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Makefile
.DS_Store
